    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301-a6">

                <pb facs="0296" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg180"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 416 of February 5, 1912, enclosing copies of telegrams exchanged
                    between the Legation and the Consulate at Foochow regarding the requirements of
                    the revolutionary authorities there in the matter of registering the property of
                    foreigners.</p>
                <p>Your action in instructing the Vice and Deputy Consul in Charge at Foochow in
                    accordance with the decision reached by the diplomatic body: that property
                    holding by foreigners is regulated by treaty provision, in which matter consuls
                    can take no action, is approved.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
